---
const checks = [
	{
		label: 'Session files',
		value: 'Interoperable',
		note: 'JSONL transcripts read and written in upstream pi’s v3 tree format — both directions.',
	},
	{
		label: 'Message wire',
		value: 'Byte-aligned',
		note: 'camelCase roles, type tags, tool call ids and stop reasons match the upstream snapshots.',
	},
	{
		label: 'Event stream',
		value: 'Frame-aligned',
		note: 'turn_start, tool lifecycles and turn_end fire in upstream order, including parallel tool results.',
	},
	{
		label: 'Configuration',
		value: 'Same shape',
		note: 'settings.json, models.json and mcp.json use the upstream layout; pi-rs keeps its own directory.',
	},
];
---

<section class="section compat">
	<div class="container compat__inner">
		<div class="compat__copy reveal">
			<span class="eyebrow">Compatibility</span>
			<h2>Drop-in for the tools you already wrote</h2>
			<p>
				pi-rs is a port, not a fork with a new contract. Sessions, transcripts and configuration keep the shapes
				upstream pi uses, so an existing script, diff harness or MCP server keeps working against the Rust
				binary.
			</p>
			<ul class="compat__list">
				<li>
					<svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
						<path d="M3 8.5l3.2 3.2L13 5" />
					</svg>
					<span>Both binaries can share a project — they read the same project-level <code class="mono">.pi/</code> resources.</span>
				</li>
				<li>
					<svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
						<path d="M3 8.5l3.2 3.2L13 5" />
					</svg>
					<span>Live diffing against upstream snapshots is part of the test suite.</span>
				</li>
				<li>
					<svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
						<path d="M3 8.5l3.2 3.2L13 5" />
					</svg>
					<span>Configuration stays isolated in <code class="mono">~/.pi-rs/agent/</code>, so the two can coexist.</span>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</div>

		<ul class="compat__matrix reveal">
			{
				checks.map((check) => (
					<li class="compat__row">
						<span class="compat__label">{check.label}</span>
						<span class="badge badge--accent">{check.value}</span>
						<p>{check.note}</p>
					</li>
				))
			}
		</ul>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.compat {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.compat__inner {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
		align-items: start;
	}

	.compat__copy h2 {
		font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4.2vw, 2.75rem);
		margin-block: 0.85rem 0.9rem;
	}

	.compat__copy > p {
		color: var(--text-muted);
		font-size: 1.02rem;
	}

	.compat__list {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.75rem;
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}

	.compat__list li {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.6rem;
		font-size: 0.93rem;
		color: var(--text-muted);
	}

	.compat__list svg {
		flex-shrink: 0;
		margin-top: 0.28rem;
		color: var(--accent);
	}

	.compat__list code {
		color: var(--text);
	}

	.compat__matrix {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}

	.compat__row {
		padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		background: var(--surface);
	}

	.compat__label {
		display: block;
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		color: var(--text-dim);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}

	.compat__row p {
		margin-top: 0.6rem;
		font-size: 0.88rem;
		color: var(--text-muted);
	}

	@media (max-width: 900px) {
		.compat__inner {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		}
	}
</style>
